hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1080","Chapter on the counsel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to armies and commanders, 1118 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Alqamah ibn Marthad narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah al-Aslami, who narrated to him, from his father, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed a commander over an army or an expedition, he would call him and counsel him regarding himself in particular and those Muslims with him with good. He would say: Campaign in the name of Allah and in the path of Allah; fight those who disbelieve in Allah. Campaign, and do not act treacherously, do not misappropriate spoils, do not mutilate, and do not kill a child. When you meet your enemy among the polytheists, call them to one of three courses - or traits - and if they answer you to any of them, accept it from them and restrain yourself from them: Call them to Islam; if they do so, inform them that they have what the Muslims have and upon them is what is upon the Muslims. Then call them to move from their abode to the abode of the Emigrants; if they do so, inform them that they have what the Emigrants have and upon them is what is upon the Emigrants. If they accept Islam and choose their own abode, inform them that they are like the Bedouin believers, subject to the ruling of Allah that applies to the believers - or he said: the Muslims - and that they have no share in the spoils or the fay'. If they refuse, call them to pay the jizyah; if they do so, accept it from them and restrain yourself from them. If they refuse, seek Allah's help and fight them. When you besiege a fortress and they want you to grant them the covenant of Allah and the covenant of His Messenger, do not grant them the covenant of Allah nor the covenant of His Messenger; grant them your own covenant and the covenant of your fathers and the covenants of your companions, for it is lighter for you to break your own covenant and the covenants of your fathers than to break the covenant of Allah and the covenant of His Messenger. And when you besiege the people of a fortress and they want you to bring them down upon the judgment of Allah, do not bring them down upon the judgment of Allah, for you do not know whether you will hit Allah's judgment concerning them; rather bring them down upon your own judgment."
